<decompilertest>
<binaryimage arch="x86:LE:32:default:windows">
<!--
    kuna issue testcase: a compare-cascade test the next test on the same
    value makes redundant is removed (`option impliedtest on|off`, default-ON).

    Issue:      kuna GH-ISSUE - an MSVC two-way switch prints as
                `if ((v1) && (v1 == 1))`.
    Stage:      P3 dataflow - the fullloop edge-removal tail
                (`p3_dataflow/kuna_impliedtest.rs`).
    P0 assert:  `option impliedtest on|off`.

    Fixture: decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/impliedtest_pe_i386.exe
    (source impliedtest_pe_i386.s, notes in impliedtest_pe_i386.txt). pick
    (0x401000) tests `sub eax,ebx; je default; sub eax,1; jne default` with
    zero kept in ebx, the shape MSVC /O2 gives `switch (r) { case 1: ...;
    case 0: default: ... }`.

    Pass 1 (`option impliedtest off`) reproduces the bug: the zero test
    prints beside the equality it is implied by.
    Pass 2 (shipped default) prints the one test, and both arms keep their
    stores and the report call.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">
c3
</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="harness_stub"/>
</binaryimage>
<script>
  <com>clear architecture</com>
  <com>load file decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/impliedtest_pe_i386.exe</com>
  <com>option impliedtest off</com>
  <com>read symbols</com>
  <com>function bounds 0x401000 as pick</com>
  <com>load function pick</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>clear architecture</com>
  <com>load file decompiler/crates/kuna-analysis/tests/fixtures/impliedtest_pe_i386.exe</com>
  <com>read symbols</com>
  <com>function bounds 0x401000 as pick</com>
  <com>load function pick</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>quit</com>
</script>
<stringmatch name="IMPLIEDTEST #1: off, the zero test prints beside the equality" min="1" max="1">if \(\(v[0-9]+\) &amp;&amp; \(v[0-9]+ == 1\)\)</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="IMPLIEDTEST #2: on, the cascade is one test" min="1" max="1">if \(v[0-9]+ != 1\)</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="IMPLIEDTEST #3: both passes keep the case 1 store" min="2" max="2">\[1\] = 0;</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="IMPLIEDTEST #4: both passes keep the default store" min="2" max="2">\[1\] = 0xf;</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="IMPLIEDTEST #5: both passes report through one call" min="2" max="2">sub_401050\(v[0-9]+,v[0-9]+\);</stringmatch>
</decompilertest>
